From 1602fafc350e670fa432cb7bbcf2edc9e53d0a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Wen <jackwen04@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:14:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Implement VK_EXT_transform_feedback

Metal has no transform feedback, so KosmicKrisp captures it the way
Honeykrisp does, on top of the poly geometry shader emulation: the GS
rasterization VS writes the captured outputs to the buffers, after the GS
count pass, its prefix sum and the pre-GS program place each primitive and
advance the buffer offsets and stream queries.

A pipeline capturing transform feedback from its VS or TES gets a
passthrough GS (poly_nir_passthrough_gs) built for its topology class at
pipeline creation; its VS owns it and binds it. Adjacency draws through it
are unrolled to lists first.

The rasterized outputs of a GS that captures are trimmed to the components
the FS reads, since Metal wants their types to match and linking keeps the
captured components. A stage feeding a GS no longer lowers its clip and cull
distances for Metal, the GS rasterization VS does.

Exposes transformFeedback, geometryStreams, queries
(VK_QUERY_TYPE_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM_EXT) and
vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT, with the limits the physical device already
reported. transformFeedbackStreamsLinesTriangles stays false.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
